&lt;h2 id="preface"&gt;Preface
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Wolfram Mathematica (abbreviated as MMA) is a &lt;strong&gt;scientific computing software&lt;/strong&gt; developed by Wolfram Research. This article introduces Mathematica&amp;rsquo;s interface, syntax, and basic applications. Similar software includes &lt;a class="link" href="https://ww2.mathworks.cn/products/matlab.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;MATLAB&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.maplesoft.com.cn/products/maple/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;Maple&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Official MMA website: &lt;a class="link" href="https://www.wolfram.com/mathematica/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;https://www.wolfram.com/mathematica/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Installation and activation guide: &lt;a class="link" href="https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/632361071" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;Mathematica Installation and Activation Tutorial - 科研小飞 (Zhihu)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This article is suitable for readers &lt;strong&gt;with basic programming knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;. However, you can skip programming-related sections if needed. All screenshots are taken from Windows 11, Mathematica 13.3. (The latest version 14.0 was released in December 2023 with backward compatibility)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="MMA version used in demonstration" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="183px" data-flex-grow="76" height="897" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/1.png" width="684"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="interface"&gt;Interface
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;After installation and activation, create a new notebook to see the following interface:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Basic MMA interface" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="211px" data-flex-grow="88" height="1302" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/2.png" srcset="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/2_hu_249c4066607da1f1.png 800w, https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/2.png 1146w" width="1146"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quick overview of MMA interface:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="MMA interface introduction" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="639px" data-flex-grow="266" height="430" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/3.png" srcset="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/3_hu_ef4922d019221d17.png 800w, https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/3.png 1146w" width="1146"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key points:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;Enter&lt;/kbd&gt; creates new lines; use &lt;kbd&gt;Shift&lt;/kbd&gt;+&lt;kbd&gt;Enter&lt;/kbd&gt; to execute code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The red triangle on the left palette also executes code; the gray square stops computations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MMA&amp;rsquo;s Notebook feature is primarily for computation rather than note-taking. Refer to official documentation for details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;kbd&gt;Ctrl&lt;/kbd&gt;+&lt;kbd&gt;Shift&lt;/kbd&gt;+&lt;kbd&gt;I&lt;/kbd&gt; to show input form (code) and &lt;kbd&gt;Ctrl&lt;/kbd&gt;+&lt;kbd&gt;Shift&lt;/kbd&gt;+&lt;kbd&gt;N&lt;/kbd&gt; for mathematical form. Detailed explanations follow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="syntax"&gt;Syntax
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Mathematica is essentially a Wolfram Language (WL) interpreter. Let&amp;rsquo;s explore basic syntax and common commands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="help-documentation"&gt;Help Documentation
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Query function documentation using &lt;code&gt;? Solve&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="help-solve" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="775px" data-flex-grow="323" height="316" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/4.png" srcset="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/4_hu_e7525e3dd6a219ff.png 800w, https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/4.png 1021w" width="1021"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;?&lt;/code&gt; operator displays brief help for any function. Click the &lt;code&gt;i&lt;/code&gt; icon for detailed documentation (prioritizes &lt;a class="link" href="https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/589034642" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;offline docs&lt;/a&gt;, falls back to &lt;a class="link" href="https://reference.wolfram.com/language/index.html.zh" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;online docs&lt;/a&gt;). Access full documentation via Help -&amp;gt; Wolfram Documentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="comments"&gt;Comments
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-mathematica" data-lang="mathematica"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;(* Comment *)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Comments use &lt;code&gt;(*&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;*)&lt;/code&gt;, similar to C/C++ &lt;code&gt;/* */&lt;/code&gt;. Examples:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;
&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-mathematica" data-lang="mathematica"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;(*Hello*)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;(*World*)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; 
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Both lines execute as &lt;code&gt;1 + 1&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="comment-test" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="333px" data-flex-grow="138" height="211" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/5.png" width="293"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="brackets"&gt;Brackets
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Master bracket usage before learning functions!&lt;br&gt;
Official reference: &lt;a class="link" href="https://reference.wolfram.com/language/howto/UseBracketsAndBracesCorrectly.html.zh" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
 &gt;Using Brackets and Braces Correctly&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Four bracket types in MMA:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id="parentheses-"&gt;Parentheses &lt;code&gt;()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Group expressions and set operation precedence:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Parentheses usage" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="470px" data-flex-grow="195" height="245" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/6.png" width="480"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id="square-brackets-"&gt;Square Brackets &lt;code&gt;[]&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Function calls and parameters:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Square bracket usage" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="466px" data-flex-grow="194" height="121" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/7.png" width="235"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id="curly-braces-"&gt;Curly Braces &lt;code&gt;{}&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Create lists:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Curly brace usage" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="735px" data-flex-grow="306" height="93" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/8.png" width="285"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;List operations will be explained later.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id="double-brackets-"&gt;Double Brackets &lt;code&gt;[[]]&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Access list elements (shorthand for &lt;code&gt;Part&lt;/code&gt; function):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Double bracket usage" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="487px" data-flex-grow="203" height="212" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/9.png" width="431"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="operations-and-expressions"&gt;Operations and Expressions
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;MMA supports basic mathematical operations:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
	&lt;thead&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Name&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Symbol&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Function Form&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Math Form&lt;/th&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/thead&gt;
	&lt;tbody&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Addition&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;a + b&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Plus[a, b]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;$a+b$&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Subtraction&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;a - b&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Subtract[a, b]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;$a-b$&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Multiplication&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;a * b&lt;/code&gt;&lt;sup id="fnref:1"&gt;&lt;a href="#fn:1" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref"&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Times[a, b]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;$a\times b$&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Division&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;a / b&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Divide[a, b]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;$\frac ab$&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Power&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;a ^ b&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Power[a, b]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;$a^b$&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Modulo&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;-&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Mod[a, b]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;$a\bmod b$&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Examples with numbers and symbols:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Numeric and symbolic operations" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="309px" data-flex-grow="129" height="331" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/10.png" width="427"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expressions&lt;/strong&gt; combine operations/function calls. MMA automatically reduces fractions and combines like terms but &lt;strong&gt;doesn&amp;rsquo;t expand expressions&lt;/strong&gt;. Use &lt;code&gt;Simplify&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;FullSimplify&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Simplification example" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="579px" data-flex-grow="241" height="239" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/11.png" width="577"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id="boolean-expressions"&gt;Boolean Expressions
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Comparisons return &lt;code&gt;True&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;False&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Equations and inequalities" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="489px" data-flex-grow="203" height="212" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/12.png" width="432"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;blockquote&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;==&lt;/code&gt; for equality checks. Single &lt;code&gt;=&lt;/code&gt; assigns variables.&lt;br&gt;
Use &lt;code&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/code&gt; for AND and &lt;code&gt;||&lt;/code&gt; for OR. Simplify with &lt;code&gt;Simplify&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;FullSimplify&lt;/code&gt;, or solve with &lt;code&gt;Solve&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;Reduce&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Boolean simplification and solving" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="176px" data-flex-grow="73" height="876" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/13.png" width="646"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="variables-and-constants"&gt;Variables and Constants
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Declare variables with &lt;code&gt;variable = value&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Variable creation" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="467px" data-flex-grow="194" height="211" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/14.png" width="411"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;All declared variables in expressions get substituted&lt;/strong&gt;. Variables can reference other variables:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Substitution example" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="407px" data-flex-grow="169" height="361" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/15.png" width="613"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use &lt;code&gt;Clear[variable]&lt;/code&gt; to unset variables:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Clear usage" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="236px" data-flex-grow="98" height="353" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/16.png" width="348"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Built-in constants&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
	&lt;thead&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Constant&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Name&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Approx. Value&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Math Form&lt;/th&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/thead&gt;
	&lt;tbody&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Pi&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Pi&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;3.141592654&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;$\pi$&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;E&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Euler&amp;rsquo;s number&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;2.718281828&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;$\mathrm e$&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;I&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Imaginary unit&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;-&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;$i$&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Infinity&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Infinity&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;-&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;$\infty$&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;Degree&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Degree&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;-&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;$\degree$&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h3 id="functions"&gt;Functions
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h4 id="invocation"&gt;Invocation
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Call functions using &lt;code&gt;FunctionName[param1, param2, ...]&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Function call 1" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="312px" data-flex-grow="130" height="425" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/17.png" width="553"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Single-parameter functions can use postfix notation &lt;code&gt;param // FunctionName&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Function call 2" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="336px" data-flex-grow="140" height="421" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/18.png" width="590"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Supports chaining:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Chained calls" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="1145px" data-flex-grow="477" height="162" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/19.png" width="773"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id="definition"&gt;Definition
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Define functions with &lt;code&gt;FunctionName[param1_, param2_, ...] := returnValue&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;strong&gt;Each parameter requires trailing underscore&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Function definition" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="549px" data-flex-grow="228" height="152" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/20.png" width="348"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;blockquote&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extension - Recursive Functions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Fibonacci sequence example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;img alt="Fibonacci sequence" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="629px" data-flex-grow="262" height="289" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/21.png" width="758"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

 &lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2 id="built-in-functions"&gt;Built-in Functions
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;MMA has nearly 6000 built-in functions&lt;sup id="fnref:2"&gt;&lt;a href="#fn:2" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref"&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;. Common ones include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="numerical-evaluation-n"&gt;Numerical Evaluation N
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;N[expr]&lt;/code&gt;: Numerical value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;N[expr, n]&lt;/code&gt;: n-digit precision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="N example" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="234px" data-flex-grow="97" height="423" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/22.png" width="414"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="trigonometric-functions"&gt;Trigonometric Functions
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;All trigonometric functions use radians. Add &lt;code&gt;Degree&lt;/code&gt; for angles:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Trigonometric functions" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="243px" data-flex-grow="101" height="423" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/23.png" width="430"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="equation-solving-solvereduce"&gt;Equation Solving Solve/Reduce
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Solve equations with &lt;code&gt;Solve&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Solve equations" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="349px" data-flex-grow="145" height="657" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/24.png" srcset="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/24_hu_ca1e37adef87e877.png 800w, https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/24.png 956w" width="956"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Solve inequalities with &lt;code&gt;Reduce&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Reduce inequalities" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="460px" data-flex-grow="191" height="485" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/25.png" srcset="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/25_hu_1914ceaac1808ab8.png 800w, https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/25.png 931w" width="931"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Reduce&lt;/code&gt; handles complex expressions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Advanced Reduce usage" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="1426px" data-flex-grow="594" height="121" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/26.png" width="719"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="alternative-solvers-nsolvefindinstance"&gt;Alternative Solvers NSolve/FindInstance
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;NSolve&lt;/code&gt;: Numerical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;FindInstance&lt;/code&gt;: Find specific solution instances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="FindInstance usage" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="751px" data-flex-grow="313" height="279" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/27.png" srcset="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/27_hu_6d18d6e8a6864f70.png 800w, https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/27.png 874w" width="874"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="optimization-maximizeminimize"&gt;Optimization Maximize/Minimize
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Minimize&lt;/code&gt; finds minima with conditions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Minimize usage" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="397px" data-flex-grow="165" height="392" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/28.png" width="650"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Maximize&lt;/code&gt; works similarly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="differentiation-d"&gt;Differentiation D
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;D[f, x]&lt;/code&gt;: First derivative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;D[f, {x, n}]&lt;/code&gt;: nth derivative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;f'[x]&lt;/code&gt;: Shorthand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Symbolic differentiation" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="614px" data-flex-grow="256" height="146" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/29.png" width="374"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="integration-integrate"&gt;Integration Integrate
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;Integrate[f, x]&lt;/code&gt;: Indefinite integral&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;Integrate[f, {x, min, max}]&lt;/code&gt;: Definite integral&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multiple integrals supported&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Definite integral example" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="1207px" data-flex-grow="503" height="154" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/30.png" width="775"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="expansion-expandexpandall"&gt;Expansion Expand/ExpandAll
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;Expand&lt;/code&gt;: Expands products and powers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;ExpandAll&lt;/code&gt;: Expands nested expressions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id="factorization-factor"&gt;Factorization Factor
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Factor[poly]&lt;/code&gt;: Factor polynomials over integers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="plotting-plotplot3d"&gt;Plotting Plot/Plot3D
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Basic plotting examples:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Plot examples" class="gallery-image" data-flex-basis="198px" data-flex-grow="82" height="1228" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 30px), (max-width: 1023px) 700px, (max-width: 1279px) 950px, 1232px" src="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/31.png" srcset="https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/31_hu_9f74299374be4c5d.png 800w, https://goodcoder666.github.io/p/mathematica-intro/31.png 1014w" width="1014"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="conclusion"&gt;Conclusion
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;When learning MMA, I struggled with fragmented tutorials online. This guide consolidates essential syntax and common pitfalls into one resource. Originally intended as a concise tutorial, it grew to 8000+ characters. Thanks for reading!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Future articles may explore Mathematica applications in mathematics and real-world problems. Stay tuned!&lt;/p&gt;
